# Schema extension: Apollo's generated Kotlin classes for these five GraphQL
# object types collide, by simple name, with the core:model domain classes of
# the same name (Venue, Session, Speaker, Room, Partner). Kotlin/Native's
# ObjC/Swift header generator disambiguates same-simple-name collisions with
# an alphabetical fully-qualified-name tie-break, so every future package
# rename risks silently flipping which side keeps the clean Swift name (see
# the 03-01 halt). Renaming Apollo's generated classes off the domain names
# removes the collision permanently, independent of package layout. This file
# must not be removed, and the target names below must stay distinct from any
# domain-model or schema-type name.
extend type Venue @targetName(name: "GraphQLVenue")
extend type Session @targetName(name: "GraphQLSession")
extend type Speaker @targetName(name: "GraphQLSpeaker")
extend type Room @targetName(name: "GraphQLRoom")
extend type Partner @targetName(name: "GraphQLPartner")
